        "on_completion": "REQUIRED\n  Le Chemin de Nancy: Nancy\n    Needs: Nancy is connected to our capital by road.\n    Gives: +5% maximum control in Nancy.\n \nOPTIONAL\n  Le Passage de Toul: Toul\n    Needs: a Castle in Toul.\n    Gives: +10% fort defence in Toul.\n \n  Les Murs de Metz: Metz\n    Needs: City Walls in Metz.\n    Gives: +0.3 garrison size in Metz.\n \n  Les Forges de Longwy: Longwy\n    Needs: Longwy's iron production at level 4; Local Smelters in Longwy.\n    Gives: +20% iron output in Longwy.\n \n  Le Sel du Saulnois: Vic-sur-Seille\n    Needs: Vic-sur-Seille's salt production at level 4.\n    Gives: +20% salt output in Vic-sur-Seille.",
        "on_persistent_completion": "",
        "on_persistent_start": "",
        "on_monthly": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "senvm_fof_bur_3",
      "name": "Flemmish Affluence",
      "desc": "",
      "icon": "ori_refined_cloth_production",
      "group": "group_6",
      "requires": [
        "senvm_fof_bur_7",
        "senvm_fof_mission_70"
      ],
      "duration_days": 0,
      "final": false,
      "notes": "",
      "manual_index": null,
      "blocks": {
        "visible": "",
        "enabled": "",
        "bypass": "",
        "highlight": "",
        "select_trigger": "",
        "modifier_while_progressing": "",
        "on_start": "",
        "on_completion": "REQUIRED\n  La Route de Lille: Lille\n    Needs: Lille is connected to our capital by road.\n    Gives: Lille becomes a proximity source of 10.\n \nOPTIONAL\n  Les Tisserands de Gand: Ghent\n    Needs: Ghent's wool production at level 4; a Cloth Guild in Ghent.\n    Gives: +20% cloth output in Ghent.\n \n  La Halle d'Ypres: Ypres\n    Needs: a Cloth Guild and a Marketplace (or better) in Ypres.\n    Gives: +20% cloth output in Ypres.\n \n  La Bourse de Bruges: Bruges\n    Needs: a Counting House and a Wharf in Bruges.\n    Gives: +20% cloth output in Bruges.\n \n  Le Hareng d'Ostende: Ostend\n    Needs: Ostend's fish production at level 4; a Fishing Village in Ostend.\n    Gives: +1% population growth for 10 years in every location we own in Flanders, about +10% population.",
        "on_persistent_completion": "",
        "on_persistent_start": "",
        "on_monthly": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "senvm_fof_bur_4",
      "name": "The Matter of Heritage",
      "desc": "",
      "icon": "cultural_ties",
      "group": "group_6",
      "requires": [],
      "duration_days": 0,
      "final": false,
      "notes": "Annexes the rest of the burgundy_area\n\nSince the different faction countries dont have to care about the other factions that space should instead be occupied by a mechanic about generating authority \n\nUnlocks the 'SOUVERAINETÉ' mechanic in the situation. That is a progress bar with decisions and french Ire.  \nThe Duke of Burgundy is a peer of France, a vassal of its king, and richer than his master. Every homage he pays is a reminder of a crown that is not his. Sovereignty measures how far the duchy has slipped from the king's grasp: in its courts, its coin, its marriages and its lands.\n \n \nHOW IT WORKS\n \nSovereignty runs from 0 to 100. It is shown in the Our Cause section of the Fate of France while we are a subject of France. The bar is blue while we are still working towards it, and turns gold when it reaches 100.\n \nAt 100 we may proclaim our sovereignty and leave the French crown's authority for good.\n \nSovereignty rises in two ways: a little every month, and through the decisions below. France can push it back with decisions of its own.\n \n \nTHE MONTHLY GAIN\n \nEvery month our Sovereignty rises by:\n \n  0.02, plus 0.08 times our share of the Burgundian lands.\n \nThe Burgundian lands are the 112 locations of Burgundy, Lorraine, Franche-Comté, Wallonia, Flanders and Alsace. Holding 14 of them gives about 0.36 a year. Holding 101 gives about 1.1 a year.\n \n  - The gain is doubled while France is at war with anyone other than us. A king at war needs his dukes.\n  - There is no gain while we are at war with France.\n \nBuying provinces in the Burgundian lands raises our share, and so speeds the monthly gain. Every province we buy from France or one of its subjects raises Crown Ire by 2.\n \n \nCROWN IRE\n \nMany of our decisions raise Crown Ire. If it reaches 100, France moves to crush us. Our Ire never falls by itself, so it can only be lowered by decisions: La Paix d'Arras and Feindre la Loyauté.\n \n \n------------------------------------------------------------\nOUR DECISIONS\n------------------------------------------------------------\n \nProclamer la Souveraineté\nProclaim Our Sovereignty\n  The duke answers to God alone.\n  Requires: Sovereignty at 100.\n  Effect: we are no longer a subject of France.\n \nRefuser l'Hommage\nRefuse Homage\n  Each new king expects the duke on his knees. Let him wait.\n  Cost: 25 authority.\n  Effect: Sovereignty +8. Crown Ire +15.\n  Once for each King of France.\n \nLe Ressort de Malines\nThe Court of Mechelen\n  Appeals from our lands will no longer be heard in Paris, but at our own court.\n  Cost: 30 authority.\n  Effect: Sovereignty +10. Crown Ire +10.\n  Once. Requires the Age of the Renaissance.\n \nBattre Monnaie Ducale\nStrike a Ducal Coin\n  A duke who mints his own coin need not borrow the king's.\n  Cost: 10 authority.\n  Effect: Sovereignty +1.5. Crown Ire +3. We gain gold. France's inflation rises.\n  Once every 5 years.\n \nLes Terres d'Empire\nThe Lands of the Empire\n  What we hold of the Emperor, the King cannot command.\n  Cost: 15 authority.\n  Effect: Sovereignty +8 times our share of locations that lie outside France. Crown Ire +3.\n  Once every 10 years.\n \nLe Mariage d'Outre-Rhin\nA Marriage Beyond the Rhine\n  A crown across the Rhine is a friend the King of France cannot overrule.\n  Cost: 10 authority.\n  Requires: a royal marriage with a ruling house outside France.\n  Effect: Sovereignty +5. Crown Ire +5.\n  Once for each such house.\n \nLa Paix d'Arras\nThe Peace of Arras\n  The king needs us more than he hates us. Name the price of peace.\n  Cost: 20 authority.\n  Requires: France is at war with a country other than us.\n  Effect: Crown Ire −25.\n  Once every 10 years.\n \nFeindre la Loyauté\nFeign Loyalty\n  Kneel, smile, and send a gift to Paris.\n  Cost: gold.\n  Effect: Sovereignty −3. Crown Ire −10.\n  Once every 3 years.\n \n \n------------------------------------------------------------\nFRANCE'S DECISIONS\n------------------------------------------------------------\n \nExiger l'Hommage\nDemand Homage\n  The new duke will kneel, as his fathers knelt.\n  Cost: 25 prestige.\n  Effect: the Duke's Sovereignty −5.\n  Once for each Duke of Burgundy.\n \nL'Appel au Parlement\nAppeal to the Parlement\n  Any subject of the duke may still appeal to the king's justice in Paris.\n  Cost: gold.\n  Effect: the Duke's Sovereignty −4.\n  Once every 15 years. Unavailable once the Duke has established Le Ressort de Malines.\n \nAcheter le Conseil\nBuy the Council\n  Every ducal councillor has a price, and the king can pay it.\n  Cost: gold.\n  Effect: the Duke's Sovereignty −2.\n  Once every 15 years.\n \nCrackdown\n  Our existing Crackdown, used against the Independentists, also lowers the Sovereignty of every Independentist member by 15.\n ",
      "manual_index": null,
      "blocks": {
        "visible": "",
        "enabled": "every country in the burgundry area (except ourselves) has more than 100 opinion of us",
        "bypass": "",
        "highlight": "",
        "select_trigger": "",
        "modifier_while_progressing": "",
        "on_start": "",
        "on_completion": "",
        "on_persistent_completion": "",
        "on_persistent_start": "",
        "on_monthly": ""
      }
    },
