    {
      "id": "senvm_fof_bur_6",
      "name": "The Ducal Heartland",
      "desc": "",
      "icon": "saharan_gold_trade",
      "group": "group_6",
      "requires": [
        "senvm_fof_mission_68",
        "senvm_fof_gk_destroy_pretenders"
      ],
      "duration_days": 0,
      "final": false,
      "notes": "\nAllows Bugundry to purchase provinces at the cost of 20x province_tax_base\nThe Provinces avaiable for purchase are provinces in the following areas \nburgundy_area  lorraine_area wallonia_area flanders_area\nfranche_comte_area and alsace_area\nthe cost is halved if the target country has more than 100 opinion of us\nwhile the AI will never open a mission tree so they will never do this. IF any country has started the fate of france situation the The burgudnian expension should be simulated anyway. \n",
      "manual_index": null,
      "blocks": {
        "visible": "",
        "enabled": "",
        "bypass": "",
        "highlight": "",
        "select_trigger": "",
        "modifier_while_progressing": "",
        "on_start": "",
        "on_completion": "HOW THESE MISSIONS WORK\n \nEach of these missions has one required quest: a road from a named location to our capital. Once that road is built and the location is ours, the mission can be taken.\n \nAll other quests are optional. Each one that is fulfilled when we take the mission pays its reward. Each one that is not is lost for good: it cannot be fulfilled later. A quest whose location we do not own cannot be fulfilled. We choose when to take the mission. Taking it early is quicker; waiting pays more.\n \nEvery fulfilled quest, the road included, also gives:\n  - +2.5 development in its location\n  - +0.0075 monthly manpower in its location\n  - +10 authority to our faction in the Fate of France, if we belong to one\n \nArtistic Development: the maximum development of the Artistic Development cabinet action is 24 + 0.5 for every quest fulfilled across all five missions: 37 if all 26 are fulfilled. Each mission we take raises it by 0.5 for every quest fulfilled when we take it. It is never lowered by these missions.\n\nREQUIRED\n  La Route de l'Yonne: Auxerre\n    Needs: Auxerre is connected to our capital by road.\n    Gives: +10% market access in Auxerre.\n \nREQUIRED\n  Le Clos de Vougeot: Beaune\n    Needs: Beaune's wine production at level 5.\n    Gives: +20% wine output in Beaune.\n \n  Le Port de Chalon: Chalon-sur-Saône\n    Needs: Chalon's wine production at level 4; a Winery in Dijon.\n    Gives: +20% wine output in Chalon-sur-Saône.\n \n  Cluny: Mâcon\n    Needs: a Monastery in Mâcon; Mâcon's wine production at level 4.\n    Gives: +20% wine output in Mâcon.\n \n  Le Safran de Dijon: Dijon\n    Needs: Dijon's saffron production at level 4.\n    Gives: +20% saffron output in Dijon.",
        "on_persistent_completion": "",
        "on_persistent_start": "",
        "on_monthly": ""
      }
    },
    {
